<p>1) What happened to the Daeva definitely fits in with the idea of <em>reality quakes</em> and I get the terminology from Kenneth Hite (who got the idea from Mary Gentle's <em>Ash, A Secret History</em>). The terminology works here and is better than some long-winded &quot;the catastrophic event that separates Daeva history from ours&quot; everytime.<br />
2) <a href="/scp-140">SCP-140</a> isn't the only copy of the <em>Chronicles</em>. Somewhere there is a copy where the Daeva aren't destroyed by Ghengis Khan, but rather six centuries later by Napoleon Bonaparte. As those other copies get filled in, Daeva history gets closer to the present, and more and more reality shards get retrocreated, like deep rock pushed up along a fault line. This is one, the Antimatter Antipope is another, along with that temple in China, and the ruins where <a href="/scp-2140">SCP-2140</a>-1-D was recovered.</p>
<p>ETA: A <a href="/tag-search">tag search</a> for &quot;daevite, scp&quot; shows that I missed a few. Of course that doesn't show articles like this one that aren't tagged (yet?).</p>

							</div>

								
